{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Presenting the Product"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Features"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 14}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange information about people's interests and backgrounds using a wider range of language."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le14ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Stressing New Information"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Giving oral presentations is essential in the business world. When presenting in English, it is important to make sure you stress important or new information. Within a sentence, you can choose to put the stress on a word that you think is new (within the context) or important to the listener."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To emphasize a word, you can change the stress from the principal word to another content word. That means that your pitch will rise and the volume will be louder on that word. This keeps the listener engaged in what you are saying and focused on the important or new facts and information. <br> By choosing a word other than the one you normally stress, you put emphasis on the new one."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you <span class=\"strong\">stress new information</span>, you pronounce new information with more breath force, since it is more prominent."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We have all been under a lot of <span class=\"strong\">pressure</span> lately."}, {"type": "example", "content": "A crisis is, indeed, a <span class=\"strong\">stressful</span> situation. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If everyone maintains the <span class=\"strong\">same</span> goals, we can overcome this."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Passive Voice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In English, the sentence structure usually follows the same sequence: <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">verb</span> + <span class=\"italic\">object</span>. The subject comes first and the object comes last. However, if you don't want to pay special attention to the subject, you can change the word order. One way of doing this is by using the passive voice to change the focus in a sentence. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The passive voice allows you talk about an event or action from the point of view of the thing or person affected. Sometimes you can write a sentence without even mentioning the agent (who or what was responsible for the action). "}, {"type": "text", "content": "This is how the passive is formed: </br><span class=\"italic\">thing receiving action </span>+<span class=\"italic\"> be</span> +<span class=\"italic\"> past participle </span>+<span class=\"italic\"> (by) </span>+<span class=\"italic\"> (thing doing action)</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "A crisis can be overcome if we maintain the same goals."}, {"type": "example", "content": "A great job was done handling the crisis. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Our company was hit hard by the bad press. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The company's profitability was affected because of the crisis."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Our client needs to be taken through all the steps."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The reason for rebranding needs to be determined. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Research is to be conducted by our specialists. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be under pressure"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used to say you feel like you have too many things to do "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We have all been under a lot of pressure lately."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le14ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear in a presentation about rebranding."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to not be out of the woods yet "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used to say that there are likely to be more difficulties before things improve"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: From a brand perspective, however, we're still not out of the woods yet."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le14ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pat ourselves on the back"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used to praise ourselves for doing something well"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I feel it's a bit too soon to be patting ourselves on the back."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le14ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "profitability "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the state of making money by selling things or doing business, after your costs have been paid "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As a result, the company's profitability was affected."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le14ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to distance"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to say that you are not involved with someone or something, especially to avoid being connected with them"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: By developing a new identity, they will distance itself from their previous identity."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le14ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "association "}, {"type": "definition", "conten